sketchBlocks.bodyMarkdown:
A read API often starts with a **collection route**. The route represents a set of resources and responds with JSON.

```js
const events = [
  { id: 1, title: "Open Mic" },
  { id: 2, title: "Career Fair" },
];

app.get("/api/events", (req, res) => {
  res.status(200).json(events);
});
```

**Line by line:** the array is deterministic in-memory data for this course. `app.get("/api/events", ...)` registers the collection endpoint. `res.status(200)` makes the successful status explicit. `.json(events)` serializes the JavaScript array and sends it with a JSON response.

Keep the route focused: it should select the data to return and construct the response, not perform unrelated work.

