sketchBlocks.bodyMarkdown:
A read API also needs routes that return one resource. Before route parameters are introduced, a fixed path is enough to see the response shape clearly.

```js
const venue = {
  id: 7,
  name: "Library Hall",
};

app.get("/api/venues/7", (req, res) => {
  res.status(200).json(venue);
});
```

**Step by step:** the path identifies one resource location, the handler selects one object, and the response sends exactly that object as JSON. The status and body together form the HTTP contract.

The next topic will replace a fixed id in the path with a route parameter so one handler can work for many resource ids.

